      "content": "thanks for the suggestion. the \"boutique-level logistical anomaly\" part sounds much more aligned with our brand voice than what actually happened.\n\nbut i'm still stuck on how to describe the \"why\" of it. it felt so weirdly specific, like the software just... had a mind of its own for a second and pulled a prank on us. i know you said that's a stretch, but is there any way to lean into that sense of a \"small, unpredictable intervention\" in a way that sounds upscale? like, instead of saying the software broke, can we make it sound like the shipment just had a momentary, inexplicable detour that felt almost... intentional or playful? i want to capture that energy without making it sound like we're incompetent or using fairy tales.",
